@@ -0,0 +1,90 @@
+# Byte-Size
+
+A fast CLI tool written in Go that displays file and directory sizes in human-readable format.
+
+Supports automatic unit selection, forced units (B, KB, MB, GB, TB, PB), SI units, JSON output, sorting, and summing.
+
+## Features
+
+- Automatic unit selection (B, KB, MB, GB, TB, PB)
+- Force specific unit with `-u`
+- SI units (1000-based) with `-si`
+- JSON output with `-json`
+- Sum multiple files/directories with `-sum`
+- Sort by size with `-sort` (ascending) or `-sort -r` (descending)
+- Quiet mode with `-q` (size only, no path)
+- Recursive directory size calculation
+- Single binary, no dependencies
+
+## Installation
+
+### From source
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/byte-size@latest
+```
+
+### Build manually
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/byte-size.git
+cd byte-size
+go build -o byte-size .
+cp byte-size /usr/local/bin/
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+byte-size [options] <path...>
+```
+
+### Options
+
+| Flag | Description |
+|------|-------------|
+| `-u UNIT` | Force unit: B, KB, MB, GB, TB, PB |
+| `-si` | Use SI units (1000-based instead of 1024-based) |
+| `-json` | Output as JSON |
+| `-sum` | Print total size of all paths |
+| `-sort` | Sort output by size (ascending) |
+| `-r` | Reverse sort order (largest first) |
+| `-q` | Quiet mode: only print the size, no path |
+
+### Examples
+
+```bash
+# Show file size
+byte-size main.go
+# main.go  5.54 KB
+
+# Show directory size in MB
+byte-size -u MB /var/log
+# /var/log  124.32 MB
+
+# Sum sizes of multiple files
+byte-size -sum *.go *.md
+# 42.17 KB
+
