+# regex-extract
+
+Extract data from files or stdin using regular expressions. Fast Go CLI with support for capture groups, named groups, JSON/CSV output, and line counting.
+
+## Features
+
+- Extract matches from files or piped stdin
+- Capture group selection (`-g 1`)
+- Named capture groups with `(?<name>...)` syntax
+- JSON and CSV output formats
+- Line number counting mode (`--count`)
+- Exit code on no match (`--exit-code`)
+- RE2 regex engine (fast, safe, no ReDoS)
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/regex-extract@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/regex-extract.git
+cd regex-extract
+go build -o regex-extract .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+regex-extract <pattern> [flags] [file...]
+```
+
+### Flags
+
+| Flag | Description |
+|------|-------------|
+| `-j, --json` | Output matches as JSON arrays |
+| `--csv` | Output matches as CSV |
+| `-g, --group N` | Only output capture group N (1-indexed) |
+| `-c, --count` | Print line numbers of matches |
+| `-n, --named` | Use named capture groups |
+| `-e, --exit-code` | Exit with code 1 if no match found |
+| `--stdin` | Read from stdin even when files are provided |
+| `-h, --help` | Show help |
+
+## Examples
+
+### Extract numbers from a file
+
+```bash
+regex-extract '[0-9]+' data.txt
+```
+
+### Extract email domains
+
+```bash
+echo "user@example.com" | regex-extract '(?<user>[^@]+)@(?<domain>[^@]+)' --named --json
+# Output: {"domain":"example.com","user":"user"}
+```
+
+### Count error lines
+
+```bash
+regex-extract 'ERROR' app.log --count
+# Output: 3
+#         17
+#         42
+```
+
+### Extract specific capture group
+
+```bash
+echo "price: $42.99" | regex-extract '\$([0-9.]+)' -g 1
+# Output: 42.99
+```
+
