+# string-manip
+
+String manipulation utilities for the command line. Convert case, generate slugs, encode/decode, and more.
+
+## Features
+
+- Case conversion: upper, lower, title, camelCase, PascalCase, snake_case, kebab-case
+- URL-friendly slug generation
+- String reversal, trimming, repetition
+- Padding (left/right) and truncation
+- Base64 encode/decode
+- URL encode/decode
+- ROT13 cipher
+- SHA-256 hashing
+- Hex encode/decode
+- Word wrap
+- Join/split lines
+- Find and replace
+- Contains check (exit code)
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/string-manip@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/string-manip.git
+cd string-manip
+go build -o string-manip .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+string-manip <command> [args] [input]
+echo "text" | string-manip <command> [args]
+```
+
+### Commands
+
+| Command | Description |
+|---------|-------------|
+| `upper` | Convert to UPPERCASE |
+| `lower` | Convert to lowercase |
+| `title` | Convert to Title Case |
+| `slug` | Convert to url-friendly-slug |
+| `camel` | Convert to camelCase |
+| `pascal` | Convert to PascalCase |
+| `snake` | Convert to snake_case |
+| `kebab` | Convert to kebab-case |
+| `reverse` | Reverse the string |
+| `trim` | Trim whitespace |
+| `repeat [N]` | Repeat string N times |
+| `pad-left [W] [C]` | Left-pad to width W |
+| `pad-right [W] [C]` | Right-pad to width W |
+| `truncate [N]` | Truncate to N chars with ellipsis |
+| `word-count` | Count words |
+| `char-count` | Count characters |
+| `base64-enc` | Base64 encode |
+| `base64-dec` | Base64 decode |
+| `url-enc` | URL encode |
+| `url-dec` | URL decode |
+| `rot13` | ROT13 cipher |
+| `hash` | SHA-256 hash (hex) |
+| `hex-enc` | Hex encode |
+| `hex-dec` | Hex decode |
+| `wrap [W]` | Word wrap to width W |
+| `join [sep]` | Join lines with separator |
+| `split [sep]` | Split by separator |
+| `replace from to` | Replace all occurrences |
+| `contains sub` | Check if contains substring |
+
+## Examples
+
+```bash
