+# time-format
+
+Convert between date and time formats from the command line. Supports 30+ formats including RFC standards, Unix timestamps, human-readable dates, ISO week numbers, and more.
+
+## Features
+
+- **30+ time formats**: RFC 3339, RFC 1123, Unix timestamps, ISO dates, and more
+- **Auto-detection**: Automatically detects input format from common patterns
+- **Unix timestamps**: Full support for seconds, milliseconds, and nanoseconds
+- **JSON output**: Detailed output with parsed time, timezone info, and Unix values
+- **Zero dependencies**: Single binary, fast execution
+
+## Installation
+
+### From source
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/time-format@latest
+```
+
+### Build manually
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/time-format.git
+cd time-format
+go build -o time-format .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+time-format [flags]
+```
+
+### Flags
+
+| Flag | Description | Default |
+|------|-------------|---------|
+| `-input` | Input time string | current time |
+| `-from` | Source format | auto-detect |
+| `-to` | Target format (required) | — |
+| `-list` | List all supported formats | — |
+| `-now` | Show current time in format | — |
+| `-json` | Output as JSON | — |
+
+### Examples
+
+**Current time in RFC 3339:**
+```bash
+time-format -now -to rfc3339
+# 2026-05-28T12:30:45+02:00
+```
+
+**Convert date to Unix timestamp:**
+```bash
+time-format -input '2024-03-15 14:30:00' -to epoch
+# 1710513000
+```
+
+**Unix timestamp to human-readable:**
+```bash
+time-format -input '1710511800' -from epoch -to human
+# Mar 15, 2024 at 2:10 PM UTC
+```
+
+**Date to datetime:**
+```bash
+time-format -input '2024-03-15' -to datetime
+# 2024-03-15 00:00:00
+```
+
+**Current time as milliseconds:**
+```bash
+time-format -now -to epochms
+# 1779922866939
+```
+
+**JSON output with details:**
