+# toml-cli
+
+A fast CLI tool for parsing and querying TOML files. Written in Go.
+
+## Features
+
+- **Simple and fast** — single binary, minimal dependencies
+- **Query values** — get specific values by dot-notation path (`section.key`)
+- **Flatten nested data** — automatically flattens tables and arrays of tables
+- **Multiple output modes** — text, JSON, key listing
+- **Exit codes** — 0 (success), 1 (parse/key error), 2 (usage error)
+
+## Installation
+
+### From source
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/toml-cli@latest
+```
+
+### Build manually
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/toml-cli.git
+cd toml-cli
+go build -o toml-cli .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+toml-cli <file.toml>                    # print all values
+toml-cli <file.toml> <key.path>         # get specific value
+toml-cli <file.toml> --keys             # list all flattened keys
+toml-cli <file.toml> -j / --json        # output as JSON
+```
+
+### Flags
+
+| Flag | Description |
+|------|-------------|
+| `-h, --help` | Show help message |
+| `-j, --json` | Output as JSON |
+| `--keys` | List all flattened keys |
+
+### Exit codes
+
+| Code | Meaning |
+|------|---------|
+| 0 | Success |
+| 1 | Parse error or key not found |
+| 2 | Usage error |
+
+## Examples
+
+### Print all values
+
+```bash
+toml-cli config.toml
+```
+
+### Get a specific value
+
+```bash
+toml-cli config.toml database.host
+# Output: localhost
+```
+
+### List all keys
+
+```bash
+toml-cli config.toml --keys
+# Output: title, owner.name, database.host, server.port, ...
+```
+
+### JSON output
+
+```bash
