+# systemd-gen
+
+Generate systemd unit files from templates or inline configuration.
+
+**systemd-gen** creates service and timer unit files with sensible defaults, security hardening, and optional templating. Perfect for quickly bootstrapping systemd configurations without memorizing all the directives.
+
+## Features
+
+- Generate service unit files with inline flags
+- Generate timer unit files with calendar specifications
+- Security hardening by default (NoNewPrivileges, ProtectSystem, ProtectHome)
+- Template initialization with `systemd-gen init`
+- Enable helper (creates symlinks)
+- Output to stdout or file
+- Customizable restart policies and targets
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+# From source
+go install github.com/TataneSan/systemd-gen@latest
+
+# Or build manually
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/systemd-gen.git
+cd systemd-gen
+go build -o systemd-gen .
+```
+
+## Quick Start
+
+```bash
+# Generate a service and print to stdout
+systemd-gen service -n myapp -e "/usr/bin/node server.js"
+
+# Generate with user and write to file
+systemd-gen service -n webapp -e "/usr/bin/python app.py" -u www-data -o webapp.service
+
+# Generate a timer
+systemd-gen timer -n cleanup -c "*:0/15" -p -o cleanup.timer
+
+# Create a template and edit
+systemd-gen init
+# ... edit service.template ...
+sudo cp service.template /etc/systemd/system/myapp.service
+sudo systemctl daemon-reload
+sudo systemctl enable --now myapp.service
+```
+
+## Commands
+
+| Command | Description |
+|---------|-------------|
+| `systemd-gen service [flags]` | Generate a service unit file |
+| `systemd-gen timer [flags]` | Generate a timer unit file |
+| `systemd-gen init [path]` | Create a sample service template |
+| `systemd-gen enable <file>` | Create symlink to enable a unit |
+| `systemd-gen start <name>` | Print command to start a unit |
+| `systemd-gen status <name>` | Print command to check unit status |
+| `systemd-gen help` | Show usage information |
+| `systemd-gen version` | Show version |
+
+## Service Flags
+
+| Flag | Required | Default | Description |
+|------|----------|---------|-------------|
+| `--name, -n NAME` | Yes | — | Service name |
+| `--exec-start, -e CMD` | Yes | — | ExecStart command |
+| `--user, -u USER` | No | — | User to run as |
+| `--env-file PATH` | No | — | EnvironmentFile path |
+| `--restart POLICY` | No | on-failure | Restart policy |
+| `--wanted-by TARGET` | No | multi-user.target | WantedBy target |
+| `--output, -o PATH` | No | stdout | Write to file |
+
+## Timer Flags
+
+| Flag | Required | Default | Description |
+|------|----------|---------|-------------|
+| `--name, -n NAME` | Yes | — | Timer name |
