+# notify-api
+
+REST API for sending notifications through multiple channels (webhook, email, Slack).
+
+## Endpoints
+
+| Method | Path | Description |
+|--------|------|-------------|
+| GET | `/health` | Health check |
+| POST | `/api/notify` | Send notification |
+
+## Quick Start
+
+### Docker
+
+```bash
+docker run -p 8080:8080 notify-api
+```
+
+### From source
+
+```bash
+go run ./cmd/main.go
+```
+
+Server starts on `:8080` by default. Override with `PORT` env var.
+
+## Usage
+
+### Send webhook notification
+
+```bash
+curl -s http://localhost:8080/api/notify \
+  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
+  -d '{
+    "channel": "webhook",
+    "to": "https://example.com/webhook",
+    "subject": "Deployment complete",
+    "body": "Version 1.2.0 deployed successfully"
+  }'
+```
+
+Response:
+```json
+{"success": true, "channel": "webhook", "message": "delivered (HTTP 200)"}
+```
+
+### Send Slack notification
+
+```bash
+curl -s http://localhost:8080/api/notify \
+  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
+  -d '{
+    "channel": "slack",
+    "to": "https://hooks.slack.com/services/T00/B00/XXX",
+    "subject": "Alert: High CPU usage",
+    "body": "CPU usage exceeded 90%"
+  }'
+```
+
+Response:
+```json
+{"success": true, "channel": "slack", "message": "delivered"}
+```
+
+### Send email notification
+
+```bash
+curl -s http://localhost:8080/api/notify \
+  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
+  -d '{
+    "channel": "email",
+    "to": "user@example.com",
+    "subject": "Weekly report",
+    "body": "Your weekly report is ready"
+  }'
+```
+
